## MODULE 9: risk.py

PURPOSE: Compute stop, target, position size, and R:R for each candidate.

```
function compute_risk(df, inds, pattern_result, cfg) -> dict:

    close = df["close"].iloc[-1]
    atr   = inds["atr"].iloc[-1]
    low20 = df["low"].iloc[-20:].min()
    high20= df["high"].iloc[-20:].max()

    pattern_type = pattern_result["type"]

    if pattern_type == "breakout":
        stop   = low20                         # below base low
        target = close + 2 × atr              # or high20 if higher

    elif pattern_type == "pullback":
        stop   = close - 1.5 × atr            # 1.5 ATR below entry
        target = high20                        # prior swing high

    elif pattern_type == "squeeze":
        stop   = close - atr                   # 1 ATR below
        target = close + 2 × atr

    else:  # no pattern — use generic
        stop   = close - atr
        target = close + 2 × atr

    stop   = max(stop, 0.01)
    risk   = close - stop
    reward = target - close

    if risk <= 0:
        return {"valid": False, "rr": 0}

    rr = reward / risk

    dollar_risk  = cfg["account_size"] × cfg["risk_per_trade_pct"]
    shares       = int(dollar_risk / risk)
    position_val = shares × close

    size_mult    = 1.0   # pass regime.size_mult from outside if needed

    return {
        "valid":          rr >= cfg["min_rr_ratio"] AND shares >= 1,
        "entry":          round(close, 2),
        "stop":           round(stop, 2),
        "target":         round(target, 2),
        "risk_per_share": round(risk, 2),
        "rr":             round(rr, 2),
        "shares":         shares,
        "position_value": round(position_val, 2),
        "dollar_risk":    round(dollar_risk, 2),
        "risk_pct":       round(risk / close × 100, 2),
    }
```

