```

Why ib_async over alternatives:
- Native async/await support — works naturally with Python asyncio
- Same interface as the well-known ib_insync (easy to find examples)
- Actively maintained (ib_insync is not)
- Full access to IB historical data, real-time quotes, order management
- If you later want to automate order entry, you already have the connection

Alternative to consider: Alpaca API (alpaca-trade-api or alpaca-py)
- Pros: free, no account required for market data, easier rate limits
- Cons: requires Alpaca brokerage account, not Interactive Brokers native
- Recommendation: stick with ib_async since you already have IB

